    73	> `U ≅ A^2` because `l` is a divisor at infinity of the source, so `ord_l` is
    74	> negative on some element of `C[x,y]`. So the centre is a component `B_j`, and
    75	> `ord_{B_j} = ord_l` as valuations of `K`. Conversely `B_j ⊄ U` makes
    76	> `ord_{B_j}` a valuation at infinity of the source, i.e. `ord_l` for a divisor
    77	> `l` on some `X`, dicritical with image `q(B_j) = D`. Equal valuations have
