/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:1:# R1 two-component splice-colouring census at `n22=1`
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:19:The colourable family is a sharpened surviving target for `PROVISIONAL` row R1 at `n22=1`. It is not an existence proof of an embedded curve, a finite cover, or a Keller map. The honest infinite direction is the linking number `n` of the two-unknot torus-link core; transposition colouring depends on `n` only through the order-six Artin action of `sigma2` on `6^3` triples, so the colouring census is finite. Higher unibranch points `A_{2p}` with `p>1` are outside the enumerated slice (§2.4).
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:77:**Lemma 2.4 (colouring types are finite).** A transposition colouring of an `s`-strand braid takes values in a set of cardinality `6^s`. The Artin action of any fixed generator is a permutation of that finite set, hence has finite order. For the F1 3-braid the action of `sigma2` on `6^3` triples has order six, so `sigma2^{2n}` depends on `n` only modulo three. Stage B below imposes the ordinary mixed twist `sigma2^{+/-2}` and is therefore independent of `n` entirely. The colouring census of the unbounded linking family is a finite list of residues, of size six, not an infinite search.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:79:The census is well below the 10,000-diagram and five-minute stop conditions. No AWS registration is required.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:134:Direct enumeration on at most five strands. The `V4 -> S4 -> S3` split of the genus-ladder census is used as an independent count on the surviving 3-braid: each transposition maps to a transposition of `S3`, Fox 3-colourings of the closed braid are the linear quotient, and transposition lifts are the two-element fibres. The Fox/lift count of labelled full-`S4` colourings of `F1` at `n=1` equals the direct count 24.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-coloring-census-grok46-20260831.md:165:F1 at `n=0` is the split link trefoil disjoint union unknot, linking zero, two points at infinity, forbidden by Chau. It is not a row of the census. Its 72 labelled `S4` colourings are the abstract 72-packet with no splice coupling; the mutation below does not treat them as legal.
