xmodel/sol-pcurvature.log:30644:   484	## 38. Differential Galois theory of the inverse
xmodel/sol-pcurvature.log:30646:   486	**(a)** The formal inverse satisfies a differential equation coming from \(DF^{-1}=(DF)^{-1}\circ F^{-1}\). If the inverse is Liouvillian / Darbouxian / has finite differential Galois group, force it to be polynomial; if not, derive a contradiction from \(J=1\) in dimension 2.
xmodel/sol-pcurvature.log:30650:   490	**(c)** The inverse’s differential equation is tautological from the chain rule. In several variables, differential Galois theory is not a finished machine (Malgrange’s Galois groupoid, etc.). Reducing to the univariate ODEs along a pencil is, again, Żołądek charts.
