xmodel/sol-pc.log:1136:xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:121:  **Isolated 8.1(iv).** Printed p.40: \(\delta p q'-(1-u)p'q=p\). Direct differentiation on the displayed \(p=\eta^5(\eta^3-1)\), \(q=\eta(\eta^3-1)\) gives leftover \(2p\), exactly as (15) prints. The printed normalization is leftover \(p\); \(q\mapsto q/2\) produces it (and \(h\mapsto h/2\) realizes the scaled top). Nonzero roots of \(p_F\) are simple, \(p_F\) is not a proper power (\(\gcd(8,5)=1\)), so \(p^i=p_F\) forces \(i=1\). Printed (f) with \(i=1\) then reads \(8/4=(3\cdot 1+5)/(3\cdot 1+1)\). The isolated ODE therefore does not force equal indices. The pair is **not** the Proposition 4.2 approximate-root tower of a Keller pair; the note says this.
